es (index).\n3777 |         index_label : str or sequence, or False, default None\n3778 |             Column label for index column(s) if desired. If None is given, and\n3779 |             `header` and `index` are True, then the index names are used. A\n3780 |             sequence should be given if the object uses MultiIndex. If\n3781 |             False do not print fields for index names. Use index_label=False\n3782 |             for easier importing in R.\n3783 |         mode : {{'w', 'x', 'a'}}, default 'w'\n3784 |             Forwarded to either `open(mode=)` or `fsspec.open(mode=)` to control\n3785 |             the file opening. Typical values include:\n3786 | \n3787 |             - 'w', truncate the file first.\n3788 |             - 'x', exclusive creation, failing if the file already exists.\n3789 |             - 'a', append to the end of file if it exists.\n3790 | \n3791 |         encoding : str, optional\n3792 |             A string representing the encoding to use in the output file,\n3793 |             defaults to 'utf-8'. `encoding` is not supported if `path_or_buf`\n3794 |             is a non-binary file object.\n3795 |         {compression_options}\n3796 | \n3797 |                May be a dict with key 'method' as compression mode\n3798 |                and other entries as additional compression options if\n3799 |                compression mode is 'zip'.\n3800 | \n3801 |                Passing compression options as keys in dict is\n3802 |                supported for compression modes 'gzip', 'bz2', 'zstd', and 'zip'.\n3803 |         quoting : optional constant from csv module\n3804 |             Defaults to csv.QUOTE_MINIMAL. If you have set a `float_format`\n3805 |             then floats are converted to strings and thus csv.QUOTE_NONNUMERIC\n3806 |             will treat them as non-numeric.\n3807 |         quotechar : str, default '\\\"'\n3808 |             String of length 1. Character used to quote fields.\n3809 |         lineterminator :