*left* has units, then the x-axis will get a Locator and\n2672 |             Formatter appropriate for the units (e.g. dates, or categorical).\n2673 | \n2674 |         align : {'center', 'edge'}, default: 'center'\n2675 |             Alignment of the base to the *y* coordinates*:\n2676 | \n2677 |             - 'center': Center the bars on the *y* positions.\n2678 |             - 'edge': Align the bottom edges of the bars with the *y*\n2679 |               positions.\n2680 | \n2681 |             To align the bars on the top edge pass a negative *height* and\n2682 |             ``align='edge'``.\n2683 | \n2684 |         Returns\n2685 |         -------\n2686 |         `.BarContainer`\n2687 |             Container with all the bars and optionally errorbars.\n2688 | \n2689 |         Other Parameters\n2690 |         ----------------\n2691 |         color : :mpltype:`color` or list of :mpltype:`color`, optional\n2692 |             The colors of the bar faces.\n2693 | \n2694 |         edgecolor : :mpltype:`color` or list of :mpltype:`color`, optional\n2695 |             The colors of the bar edges.\n2696 | \n2697 |         linewidth : float or array-like, optional\n2698 |             Width of the bar edge(s). If 0, don't draw edges.\n2699 | \n2700 |         tick_label : str or list of str, optional\n2701 |             The tick labels of the bars.\n2702 |             Default: None (Use default numeric labels.)\n2703 | \n2704 |         label : str or list of str, optional\n2705 |             A single label is attached to the resulting `.BarContainer` as a\n2706 |             label for the whole dataset.\n2707 |             If a list is provided, it must be the same length as *y* and\n2708 |             labels the individual bars. Repeated labels are not de-duplicated\n2709 |             and will cause repeated label entries, so this is best used when\n2710 |             bars also differ in style (e.g., by passing a list to *color*.)\n2711 | \n2712 |         xerr, yerr : float